  "body": "Stacked on #2542 (#2462): review the second commit, `feat(model): a linked model is imported again when its source file changes`. This PR goes back to `main` alone when #2542 merges.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **A model records its source file.** An import from a file records the path and the file's SHA-256 (`schema::ModelSource`, `crates/app/src/model_source.rs`). The record rides `ImportModel`, `UpdateModel` (traded with the facets; undo restores it; a repair keeps it), `DeleteEntity` and `ImportFixture`. A mesh handed in, a browser pick and a generated fixture mesh record none.\n- **Project v72.** A model row may have `source: {path, sha256}` (`project/source_dto.rs`). A v71 file steps up unchanged and opens unlinked. A source on a row that is not a model, an empty path, a bad digest or an unknown key is a corrupt file. An older CamCraft refuses a v72 file by name (`unsupported project version 72`).\n- **The check** (`crates/ui/src/model_link_watch.rs`). In the window, each linked file is checked about once a second; the frame timer comes back for it while a model is linked. A file is read again only when its size or time moved. A new digest imports the file again through `CommandKind::ImportFile`, and `finish_import` lands a linked file on its model by name. This is the existing re-import: one `UpdateModel`, one undo step, the operations go Stale. **Nothing regenerates or posts.**\n- **An undo of that import stays.** The check does not import the same bytes again; only a new change imports.\n- **A missing or unreadable file** keeps the model as it is and is said on the status line one time.\n- **Unlink.** The Browser's model menu has \"Unlink from <file>\" (`CommandKind::UnlinkModel`, `SetModelSource`, one undo step). The MCP tool `set_model_link` links (to a path, its digest recorded now, no import) or unlinks (`null`). `get_job` shows `models[].source`.\n- **SHA-256** is the kernel's FIPS 180-4 code, re-exported as `camcraft_geometry::solidcraft::sha256_hex` (native only). No new crate dependency.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/2463-linked-model.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\nLive app, debug build, macOS: `camcraft-ui --mcp-port 7921 bracket.stl` (a 40 x 20 x 10 box).\n\n- Before: `get_job` gives `bracket`, bounds max (40, 20, 10), `source.sha256` `00ee0c922a5b…`.\n- The file is written again as a 40 x 20 x 25 box. Seven seconds later: bounds max (40, 20, 25), `source.sha256` `0158db27604b…`. No refusal in the log.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/model_link.rs`:\n- `an_import_from_a_file_links_the_model_to_that_file`\n- `an_update_trades_the_link_and_undo_restores_it`\n- `delete_and_undo_keep_the_link`\n- `link_and_unlink_are_one_undo_step_each_and_refuse_by_name`\n- `the_project_file_keeps_the_link_and_a_v71_file_opens_unlinked` (also: a v73 file is refused by name)\n- `a_malformed_source_row_is_refused_as_corrupt`\n- `the_mcp_tool_links_and_unlinks_and_get_job_shows_the_source`\n\n`crates/ui/src/model_link_tests.rs`:\n- `a_changed_file_is_imported_again_as_one_undo_step_and_its_operations_only_go_stale` (a generated Face operation goes Stale, no generation starts, undo restores it and stays)\n- `a_missing_file_keeps_the_model_and_is_said_one_time`\n- `unlink_stops_the_check_and_undo_links_again`\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick` after merging upstream main (da87fa5b5): 887 steps, 0 failed (ui lib suite: 1212 passed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-geometry --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Changes to tests outside this feature\n\n- `crates/app/tests/continuous_4axis_part.rs`: the test imports its model from a file, so the model is now linked and the saved example would carry this machine's absolute path. The test unlinks the model before it saves; the committed example names no file. `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj` is written again (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1`): only `\"version\"` changes. Upstream main has the file at version 70 and `PROJECT_VERSION` 71; the strict compare compares `\"version\"` too, so the test is expected to fail there (not run on main here).\n- `crates/app/tests/sketch_project.rs`: `assert_eq!(PROJECT_VERSION, 71)` is now `const { assert!(PROJECT_VERSION >= 71) }`. The DXF profile row still arrives at v71; a later step does not break the test.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows and Linux: not run. The check uses std file metadata only.\n- A window that the operating system reports as occluded does not draw frames (existing behaviour), so the check waits until the window is shown.\n- A file renamed or moved away reads as missing; link it again with `set_model_link`. There is no \"Link to file…\" item in the window yet.\n\n## Why\n\nSolidcraft proposes \"Send to CamCraft\" (tangency-labs/solidcraft#18936, Solidcraft RFC 0001 phases 1 and 3). Each save in Solidcraft writes the `.sc` file again; with this, CamCraft updates the part after each save.\n\nProcess change: yes (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`: the `set_model_link` row).\nChangelog: A model imported from a file is linked to it: when the file changes, the model is imported again (one undo step; its operations go Stale). Unlink from the Browser's model menu (#2463).\nEffort: high\nFork synced at v0.24.0 (upstream main da87fa5b5 merged in; the project version is 72, as #2441, #1517, #2016 and #1862 took 68 to 71).\n\nFixes #2463\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01MLU9aif5zm7mure23AKftd\n",
